if BN wins the people win that is the  campaign message from barisa National  the national front wooing voters with  Promises of stability and prosperity  the right-wing Coalition had ruled  Malaysia since Independence in 1957 but  anger about government corruption led to  its first defeat in the last general  election  we have to tackle this perception manage  this perception getting rid of  corruption is something barusa National  is committed to it's not just a rhetoric  the allegations tamed many of its top  politicians including leader Ahmad zahid  hamidi who's on trial for money  laundering and bribery  former chairman najib Raza who served as  prime minister for nearly 10 years has  been jailed for corruption linked to the  Looting of State investment fund 1mdb he  faces more trials in connection with the  multi-billion dollar Financial scandal  both men say that victims of political  persecution  the Coalition returned to power in 2020  after defections led to the collapse of  the then-ruling alliance since then it  has won two State polls and several by  elections buoyed by this its leaders  pushed for early elections but analysts  say corruption remains an important  issue for voters in many voters still  realize that the change that came in  2018 the court cases and the final  jailing of former prime minister najib  Raza is just the beginning of what is  supposed to be an ongoing process of  cleaning up government and putting  things back in order that job is  unfinished economists say Malaysians  will be paying the price of corruption  for years to come  it destroyed the confidence that you  have on institutions and I think the  moral corruption is much bigger impact  because more long-lasting one plus is  broken tour again is very difficult  opposition politicians have capitalized  on this warning that a vote for the  national front is a vote for corruption  this is the first time voters will have  a choice between more than two strong  coalitions surveys suggest no one party  will secure a simple majority on its own  a hung Parliament means alliances will  have to be forged and that means not  only is this election too close to call  but it would be unwise to rule out any  possibilities  Florence Louis Al Jazeera Kuala Lumpur
 

